 ],
 "notes": "Configurable module: optional capabilities (ACL, ownership, logging, object lock, website, tiering, metrics, CORS, lifecycle) are off by default, so they are checked as declared, and each must be conditional: a separate resource must be count/for_each-gated, an inline aws_s3_bucket form must be a dynamic block. sse_none_disables looks for a lower-case 'none' token (Terraform nulls render as 'None', which must not count). Only control_object_ownership, bucket_logging and object_lock_enabled are named variables in the prompt. Versioning/MFA-delete 'disabled by default' is not checked: omitting versioning entirely is a valid way to meet it and the interpreter cannot express 'no versioning resource is Enabled' when zero may exist (removed 1 check after candidate review). Candidate review 2026-11-11: DSV4F uses bucket_prefix (bucket_default_name kept: a prefix does not give the stated name); GLM53F uses data.aws_caller_identity.id as the ACL owner, which is an account ID, not the canonical user ID (acl_canonical_user_fallback kept)."
}